| Learning through work and community living. Eg-<br>Spinning and handicrafts in schools. | Learning through art, music, poetry, and<br>interaction with nature. Eg- Santiniketan model. |
| Education aimed at national reconstruction. | Education aimed at universal human development. |

**Difference Between Gandhi and Tagore on NATIONALISM**

| Mahatma Gandhi | Rabindranath Tagore |
| --- | --- |
| Advocated ethical and mass-based nationalism. | Advocated humanist and internationalist<br>nationalism. |
| Nationalism rooted in moral discipline and<br>sacrifice. | Nationalism is subordinated to universal human<br>values. |
| Used mass mobilisation and symbols to unite<br>people. Eg- Khadi, charkha, Salt Satyagraha. | Criticised ritualistic nationalism and emotional mass<br>conformity |
| --- | --- |
| Supported direct political action and non-violent<br>resistance. Eg- Non-Cooperation, Civil<br>Disobedience. | Preferred cultural regeneration over political<br>agitation. Eg- Emphasis on literature and education. |

