ong all sections of the Indian people to see the end of British rule. Though the revolt was short-lived, British realized it would be difficult for them to continue their rule in India. The army which was one of the major sources of power of British rule had turned against them. Thus, royal naval mutiny became the last nail in the coffin of British rule in India.
